      "eer": 0.3,
      "delta": 0.016666666666666663,
      "note": "Transitions and metrics alone. The complement of the row above: together they say how much of the CSBG is carried by which language a class takes versus how the speaker moves between them."
    },
    {
      "name": "cohort z-norm removed",
      "scope": "csbg",
      "eer": 0.26666666666666666,
      "delta": -0.016666666666666663,
      "note": "Raw LLRs are not comparable across claimed speakers: an unusual speaker produces large-magnitude scores for everyone. Expect this row to read ~0 on a single branch and still matter in fusion. EER is rank-based, so a per-speaker rescale only moves it by *reordering* speakers against each other -- which needs the population to vary in score scale in the first place. Fusion is not rank-based: it adds the branch to others on a shared [0, 1] scale, where the shift is exactly what makes the sum comparable. A near-zero delta here alongside a large one in the configuration table is the expected shape, not a contradiction."
    }
